# Contour Lines

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:plotly_ex, "~> 0.3"},
  {:kino, "~> 0.18"}
])
```

## Section

`contours: %{coloring: "lines"}` renders only the contour lines, colour-coded
by value using the chosen `colorscale:`. The fill is transparent.
Combine with `line: %{width: 2}` to make the lines more visible.

```elixir
alias Plotly.{Figure, Contour}

z = for i <- 0..19 do
  for j <- 0..19 do
    :math.sin(i * :math.pi() / 10) * :math.cos(j * :math.pi() / 10)
  end
end

Figure.new()
|> Figure.add_trace(
  Contour.new(
    z: z,
    colorscale: "Jet",
    contours: %{coloring: "lines"},
    line: %{width: 2}
  )
)
|> Figure.update_layout(title: "Contour Lines Only (coloring: \"lines\")")
|> Plotly.show()
```
